fe48579b'::uuid, 'Layer federalism and Centralized federalism', FALSE, 1),('12420733-a1e1-4bc0-85e6-a5beb9c6aea2'::uuid, '64c9fa47-92a8-4796-85ad-f4f1fe48579b'::uuid, 'Unitary federalism and Confederal federalism', FALSE, 2),('f7492df0-5bc0-4ea2-8a6a-29f5022be03e'::uuid, '64c9fa47-92a8-4796-85ad-f4f1fe48579b'::uuid, 'Judicial federalism and Legislative federalism', FALSE, 3),('13ad64b0-3535-45e2-8db9-6239632ec8c8'::uuid, 'e1d6ac3f-8924-4d39-8669-9029f4dcb09f'::uuid, 'It protects local jurisdictions from federal overreach and allows local laws to reflect local needs', TRUE, 0),('456238b7-0df9-46f9-8e07-c161b265f226'::uuid, 'e1d6ac3f-8924-4d39-8669-9029f4dcb09f'::uuid, 'It ensures full cooperation between federal and state governments in all programs', FALSE, 1),('1ab1fc6e-60d9-4e6d-825a-e0086bb44b29'::uuid, 'e1d6ac3f-8924-4d39-8669-9029f4dcb09f'::uuid, 'It centralizes all policymaking to achieve uniformity across states', FALSE, 2),('68ef3d31-9cc7-438e-83f0-af0f60eb7550'::uuid, 'e1d6ac3f-8924-4d39-8669-9029f4dcb09f'::uuid, 'It eliminates tensions between state and federal governments', FALSE, 3),('4eb89317-5017-4862-8a79-8c8a4c51de34'::uuid, '4d028e64-ac90-4ee5-8f43-bbd1f2ec247b'::uuid, 'It leads to tensions and reduced cooperation between federal and state governments', TRUE, 0),('394071de-5bc5-4ded-815b-2b55968742f5'::uuid, '4d028e64-ac90-4ee5-8f43-bbd1f2ec247b'::uuid, 'It guarantees equal policies across all states', FALSE, 1),('2e1fc255-c1b4-4710-8218-186ec47944ad'::uuid, '4d028e64-ac90-4ee5-8f43-bbd1f2ec247b'::uuid, 'It removes state authority entirely', FALSE, 2),('e18285d9-5ac4-48cf-8f51-307facf20a2b'::uuid, '4d028e64-ac90-4ee5-8f43-bbd1f2ec247b'::uuid, 'It prevents any local laws from existing', FALSE, 3),('c2b87be4-5d56-4479-8283-cd6de56db00c'::uuid, '5aef9c50-654f-458d-8aed-a249151a9820'::uuid, 'Marble-cake federalism', TRUE, 0),('78bb629b-c6b9-4d44-82c5-3f2b6382127b'::uuid, '5aef9c50-654f-458d-8aed-a249151a9820'::uuid, 'Layer-cake federalism', FALSE, 1),('0a74070a-8245-44bd-8c8e-35704b13777d'::uuid, '5aef9c50-654f-458d-8aed-a249151a9820'::uuid, 'Pyramid federalism', FALSE, 2),('375e5766-6b6a-4949-8ccc-e54c1e57eef9'::uuid, '5aef9c50-654f-458d-8aed-a249151a9820'::uuid, 'Flat federalism', FALSE, 3),('6defa008-a371-4f78-8958-24ca1b69d451'::uuid, 'ebe5afd0-6807-464c-8740-ee5c94ab68e6'::uuid, 'National and state governments work together to provide services efficiently', TRUE, 0),('5e011429-2ddd-409a-8abb-c9b2fd433a94'::uuid, 'ebe5afd0-6807-464c-8740-ee5c94ab68e6'::uuid, 'States lose all incentives to cooperate with the federal government', FALSE, 1),('be2be286-df1c-47f8-80e7-b2ba16273fcd'::uuid, 'ebe5afd0-6807-464c-8740-ee5c94ab68e6'::uuid, 'States can no longer influence program implementation', FALSE, 2),('11ace606-e7c8-413c-8ad2-6217730feda1'::uuid, 'ebe5afd0-6807-464c-8740-ee5c94ab68e6'::uuid, 'Cooperation always eliminates state powers entirely', FALSE, 3),('0cfac19e-9c38-4ae2-8b07-4cd0287ed149'::uuid, '4dd0b98f-f7ca-4765-8fe3-09e56d570b7d'::uuid, 'A written and supreme federal constitution', TRUE, 0),('afca5ddc-42a4-4f02-87f2-78f233cf57ee'::uuid, '4dd0b98f-f7ca-4765-8fe3-09e56d570b7d'::uuid, 'Complete interchangeability of central and state authority', FALSE, 1),('2f605fe9-08fc-4295-898f-b11d5559c5b3'::uuid, '4dd0b98f-f7ca-4765-8fe3-09e56d570b7d'::uuid, 'Absence of any special judiciary for constitutional disputes', FALSE, 2),('1b59781d-5f9f-4a12-870d-098deb10aa8a'::uuid, '4dd0b98f-f7ca-4765-8fe3-09e56d570b7d'::uuid, 'Unilateral revocability of state powers by the center', FALSE, 3),('efeae1f3-aaf7-459e-8fd4-cf2117f9d015'::uuid, '4053bb57-f92f-4605-8ae7-d5b0d965154c'::uuid, 'Political power is constitutionally divided between the federal government and the states', TRUE, 0),('9c46941a-04c7-48b6-8e00-eaa8e1168d6e'::uuid, '4053bb57-f92f-4605-8ae7-d5b0d965154c'::uuid, 'The federal government alone controls all legislative, executive and financial functions', FALSE, 1),('59af3a83-9638-4e7a-8aea-1d61b1f09967'::uuid, '4053bb57-f92f-4605-8ae7-d5b0d965154c'::uuid, 'States have no power to deal directly with their citizens', FALSE, 2),('09b23ed1-63ea-4834-86b3-a63d08b78f85'::uuid, '4053bb57-f92f-4605-8ae7-d5b0d965154c'::uuid, 'Division of power is normally informal and unwritten', FALSE, 3),('ccc01078-8189-4ad8-869e-f0be6c5a7c1b'::uuid, '0b253efb-bcf5-4be2-819f-12d635ddd195'::uuid, 'Local governments are creations of the center and may be revoked by the center', TRUE, 0),('7376a92a-2a59-44fa-8c0f-05bb3dd928a4'::uuid, '0b253efb-bcf5-4be2-819f-12d635ddd195'::uuid, 'States derive authority from a federal constitution and cannot be unilaterally changed by the center', FALSE, 1),('db7d5f19-602b-4294-8860-08ed7457490b'::uuid, '0b253efb-bcf5-4be2-819f-12d635ddd195'::uuid, 'Local governments have constitutionally guaranteed autonomy from the center', FALSE, 2),('6f76bd0a-8f0b-43e3-81db-a4d4a07eecbb'::uuid, '0b253efb-bcf5-4be2-819f-12d635ddd195'::uuid, 'A decentralized system always equalizes powers between center and units', FALSE, 3),('18081f0f-4f83-4a62-815b-71b446558f74'::uuid, 'cd33edce-67e1-4958-837b-d3cd2461f7f8'::uuid, 'To protect the spirit of the agreement and prevent the central government from easily curtailing state autonomy', TRUE, 0),('c6e870a8-e8a8-4ad1-812c-f08747d230e5'::uuid, 'cd33edce-67e1-4958-837b-d3cd2461f7f8'::uuid, 'To allow the center to change state autonomy at its discretion', FALSE, 1),('193d8d88-e2a1-4473-8b22-bd65fcae2090'::uuid, 'cd33edce-67e1-4958-837b-d3cd2461f7f8'::uuid, 'To ensure the constitution is frequently amended by the national legislature', FALSE, 2),('c4ad21f7-bac9-4e68-88b5-411d43cae9be'::uuid, 'cd33edce-67e1-4958-837b-d3cd2461f7f8'::uuid, 'To prevent the existence of any special judiciary', FALSE, 3),('c5a0b2a9-9555-4704-8446-9f8922a8ddbc'::uuid, '59b44b18-676d-4f43-8a4b-37ae0b44da85'::uuid, 'To adjudicate constitutional disputes and act as custodian of the constitution', TRUE, 0),('2b023600-f180-4975-806a-9c75ecc6f0e7'::uuid, '59b44b18-676d-4f43-8a4b-37ae0b44da85'::uuid, 'To make all regional laws without reference to the constitution', FALSE, 1),('94632bbb-1433-44c5-8127-9fe0ca41c3f5'::uuid, '59b44b18-676d-4f43-8a4b-37ae0b44da85'::uuid, 'To act as an advisory body with no power to declare laws invalid', FALSE, 2),('a21c5c01-5b41-4b34-88d4-5423c728430e'::uuid, '59b44b18-676d-4f43-8a4b-37ae0b44da85'::uuid, 'To be subordinate to regional legislatures in constitutional matters', FALSE, 3),('98c7ae39-f3ea-4ff1-85f4-25f3dd010501'::uuid, '2967628a-ddcf-4b69-8e4e-05ab2b95bb7a'::uuid, 'Increasing citizen participation by providing dual levels of government', TRUE, 0),('eb55661c-d8e0-4928-80f2-375813ac6149'::uuid, '2967628a-ddcf-4b69-8e4e-05ab2b95bb7a'::uuid, 'Guaranteeing identical policies and spending across all states', FALSE, 1),('e975023f-d2cb-4a0f-80d1-a0e1ba40ba84'::uuid, '2967628a-ddcf-4b69-8e4e-05ab2b95bb7a'::uuid, 'Eliminating any possibility of conflict between central and state governments', FALSE, 2),('3424a0df-86d3-4c61-8a50-b6a76bcccc97'::uuid, '2967628a-ddcf-4b69-8e4e-05ab2b95bb7a'::uuid, 'Removing any role for local governments in decision-making', FALSE, 3),('48093b2e-40b6-4311-8a88-052d0accfa09'::uuid, '6fb42433-bb2f-4ad8-8811-9588c6fa7d62'::uuid, 'Regional inequalities between states in areas like education funding', TRUE, 0),('adc00b9c-6a73-4e71-83ab-e2a95684bfa4'::uuid, '6fb42433-bb2f-4ad8-8811-9588c6fa7d62'::uuid, 'Mandatory uniformity of taxation across all states', FALSE, 1),('343db3b9-25d2-4f68-864f-070334f66a04'::uuid, '6fb42433-bb2f-4ad8-8811-9588c6fa7d62'::uuid, 'Complete removal of state courts'' authority', FALSE, 2),('7d1aa12c-ba83-44bc-860f-7c52f5fbc800'::uuid, '6fb42433-bb2f-4ad8-8811-9588c6fa7d62'::uuid, 'Automatic elimination of regional identities', FALSE, 3),('ba84119a-c02d-454c-80f1-b046dff76127'::uuid, '9b6336be-44ab-4e7f-82e0-9e17d6f9c74c'::uuid, 'By promoting strong regionalism that may put one region against another', TRUE, 0),('9825dce2-3818-4a83-8367-17a2c5013be7'::uuid, '9b6336be-44ab-4e7f-82e0-9e17d6f9c74c'::uuid, 'By forcing all regions to adopt the same cultural practices', FALSE, 1),('bf1f9349-15bc-49ee-8a1c-1c8272ecb361'::uuid, '9b6336be-44ab-4e7f-82e0-9e17d6f9c74c'::uuid, 'By eliminating regional governments altogether', FALSE, 2),('37588090-d319-4e43-8035-45db6a7e06a6'::uuid, '9b6336be-44ab-4e7f-82e0-9e17d6f9c74c'::uuid, 'By legally banning expressions of regional identity', FALSE, 3),('279a69d5-2751-403b-8034-f0486393653e'::uuid, 'b0a06860-1fbd-4678-822c-515970896aff'::uuid, 'Power division between states and the federal government regulated by the constitution', TRUE, 0),('7eaacf14-2670-410f-8591-868762010fa2'::uuid, 'b0a06860-1fbd-4678-822c-515970896aff'::uuid, 'Absence of any federal constitution specifying powers', FALSE, 1),('ba6e5e45-e33f-4596-8291-870677d4c894'::uuid, 'b0a06860-1fbd-4678-822c-515970896aff'::uuid, 'Complete subordination of states to the federal center', FALSE, 2),('86bef464-69b7-43c4-850f-b3286fef798d'::uuid, 'b0a06860-1fbd-4678-822c-515970896aff'::uuid, 'No recognition of nation, nationalities and peoples in representation', FALSE, 3),('1f8248b4-1726-4cdc-8b36-77509e20b9ab'::uuid, '72b50214-18b5-4a1b-8f1e-a0cfa9242523'::uuid, 'House of People''s Representatives and House of Federation', TRUE, 0),('e572da9b-bb19-4c91-81cc-c479b3c1319c'::uuid, '72b50214-18b5-4a1b-8f1e-a0cfa9242523'::uuid, 'Senate and Council of States', FALSE, 1),('b4b67ae1-6133-4640-86e2-d94097099f15'::uuid, '72b50214-18b5-4a1b-8f1e-a0cfa9242523'::uuid, 'National Assembly and Federal Council', FALSE, 2),('d80855b8-4d63-48e3-8062-3cc4b57e35ca'::uuid, '72b50214-18b5-4a1b-8f1e-a0cfa9242523'::uuid, 'House of Commons and House of Lords', FALSE, 3),('f7c666c4-a89c-4b9f-89b4-f6144b11140a'::uuid, 'a0036493-d61d-453a-803a-88ec3624222e'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('0e8ab63b-fab2-4cfe-8d51-43f3021976d9'::uuid, 'a0036493-d61d-453a-803a-88ec3624222e'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('bf13d0b6-e855-4dc7-827a-c24fd0811880'::uuid, '5b6235f3-39a3-420a-8521-c512dedde13d'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('6383e16c-7ac5-485e-8e28-6b02196183e4'::uuid, '5b6235f3-39a3-420a-8521-c512dedde13d'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1),('b452e267-c1f0-4490-8a15-9a692efc0b6d'::uuid, 'eeb33299-a004-470c-8e32-5d3d1563dd33'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('4b682f4a-558f-459b-8da9-fd0da684f978'::uuid, 'eeb33299-a004-470c-8e32-5d3d1563dd33'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1),('837a6852-ecc4-4d61-8c79-68427ffb87b1'::uuid, 'b33b0ff1-08e7-40bd-8394-b49f9912a722'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('620077ca-86a8-4d1e-8ab3-b842fd6dbf08'::uuid, 'b33b0ff1-08e7-40bd-8394-b49f9912a722'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question_id = EXCLUDED.question_id, choice_text = EXCLUDED.choice_text, is_correct = EXCLUDED.is_correct, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
INSERT INTO public.quizzes (id, subject, unit, title, description) VALUES ('a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'Citizenship', 'Unit 6', 'Molarum Grade 10 — Citizenship Citizenship Unit 6: Human Rights', 'Source-grounded Molarum Grade 10 Citizenship questions for Citizenship Unit 6: Human Rights.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET subject = EXCLUDED.subject, unit = EXCLUDED.unit, title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, quiz_id, question_type, question_text, correct_answer, explanation, order_index) VALUES ('e4999611-7290-4b5e-88be-df5478d0b308'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which statement best reflects the concept of human rights presented in the lesson?', 'They are fundamental entitlements that belong to every person simply for being human.', 'The text defines human rights as fundamental entitlements belonging to every human being without discrimination, based solely on being human.', 0),('f7fa04bd-693b-45ab-8fd9-ab2d29605772'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the unit, what do human rights provide?', 'Minimum standards indispensable for a worth-living life', 'The text states that human rights provide the minimum standards indispensable for people to live a worth-living life and to live with dignity and equality.', 1),('dcedbb73-0c93-4f83-89e4-037521f4eb4d'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What does universalism of human rights mean in this lesson?', 'They apply equally to all people everywhere and are not time-limited.', 'Universalism means human rights apply equally to all people everywhere, with no time limit, while respecting diversity.', 2),('62709aef-3370-4e24-87c3-c3389aa85a22'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'When, according to the text, do individuals stop enjoying their human rights?', 'At natural death', 'Eternality means individuals enjoy their human rights until the time of natural death.', 3),('e19ff584-2a25-4ab4-8f49-baa8d3ed11ae'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which statement best captures the inalienability of human rights as explained in the unit?', 'They are inherent to human existence, though some may be lawfully restricted in specific circumstances.', 'Inalienability means rights are inherent to all humans; some can be suspended or restricted in particular situations (e.g., curfew in emergencies, loss of liberty after conviction).', 4),('951eecf2-3827-433b-856d-a4af60447507'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which example from the text illustrates the indivisible and interdependent nature of human rights?', 'Progress in civil and political rights makes it easier to exercise economic, social and cultural rights.', 'The unit explains that rights are intrinsically connected; advancing one set (civil and political) facilitates others (economic, social, cultural).', 5),('0f5fad86-8c36-4739-8476-8c4ee7193381'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What does the inviolability of human rights imply according to the lesson?', 'They are expected not to be violated or even restricted by anyone.', 'The text states that by their nature human rights are expected not to be violated or even restricted, with some countries extending this logic even during emergencies.', 6),('204e3a97-89ab-4a21-87c1-489d0871f5a4'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'In this unit, what is meant by human rights being irrevocable?', 'They cannot be taken away by any power or authority.', 'Human rights are described as irrevocable because they originate from the social nature of humans and belong to a person simply for being human.', 7),('ebb1e294-51dd-46ad-8076-d5b62b4812f6'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following is identified in the text as a first generation (civil and political) right?', 'Freedom from torture and from cruel, inhuman, or degrading treatment', 'First generation rights include civil and political rights such as freedom from torture, as listed in the unit.', 8),('d1e0bb62-237e-4d73-8758-13839d203187'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which right is listed as a second generation (economic, social, and cultural) right?', 'Right to work', 'Second generation rights include economic, social, and cultural rights such as the right to work and education.', 9),('1c829af1-dd28-4c24-8c64-f95d721622ea'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which right is identified as part of the third generation of rights in the unit?', 'Right to political, economic, social, and cultural self-determination', 'The third generation includes rights such as self-determination and the right to development, as described in the text.', 10),('87e49887-cff8-46b0-8f5a-a7402505caf9'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What does the lesson state about universality and cultural diversity?', 'Universality does not threaten diversity and allows states to define higher standards.', 'The text clarifies that universality is not synonymous with uniformity and that states may apply higher, more specific standards beyond the minimums.', 11),('0253e3c7-e231-4460-8c1f-3933187bbbfd'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which principle is expressly articulated in Article 10 of the FDRE Constitution as highlighted in the unit?', 'Human rights and freedoms, emanating from the nature of mankind, are inviolable and inalienable.', 'The unit quotes Article 10 stating that human rights and freedoms are inviolable and inalienable because they emanate from the nature of mankind.', 12),('e26e55be-f858-4efe-8c2d-08629dc490fe'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the unit, which articles of the FDRE Constitution are named “Human Rights”?', 'Articles 14–28', 'The text states that Articles 14–28 are named “Human Rights,” while Articles 29–44 are “Democratic Rights.”', 13),('7e9a6593-82fb-40ad-8e32-1feca5c5e3a4'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the unit’s discussion of Article 10 of the FDRE Constitution, human rights and freedoms emanating from the nature of mankind are described as what?', 'Inviolable and inalienable', 'The narrative discussion states that Article 10 describes human rights and freedoms emanating from the nature of mankind as inviolable and inalienable.', 14),('d7f90740-7c1b-45fa-8f5f-977d41553de4'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which is identified in the lesson as an obligation of citizens in realizing human rights?', 'Respect for religious equality', 'The unit lists citizen obligations including respect for religious equality, gender equality, others’ rights, and the national flag.', 15),('82414da8-8d0f-4f73-88c3-1e62a4dce9fc'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'How should individuals exercise their rights according to the lesson?', 'With due regard for the rights of others', 'The unit states that individuals have a responsibility to exercise their rights with due regard for the rights of others and the community.', 16),('74f18bce-efae-4349-89d3-7a8ed87c25d5'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which action would violate the state’s obligation to respect human rights as explained in the unit?', 'Performing medical experiments on persons with disabilities without their consent', 'Under the obligation to respect, states must refrain from interfering with rights, including not conducting non-consensual medical experiments on persons with disabilities.', 17),('80c1fa83-1405-413b-8278-d8f9dab995dd'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What does the state’s obligation to protect require, according to the lesson?', 'Acting against abuses by non-state actors and ensuring access to remedies', 'The obligation to protect requires the state to prevent and remedy abuses by non-state actors, enact legislation, act when aware of threats, and ensure impartial remedies.', 18),('a62961bc-8c5f-4701-8cf1-092a8561c6bc'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which measure exemplifies the state’s obligation to fulfill the right to education in the unit?', 'Setting up enough public schools or hiring and remunerating adequate numbers of teachers', 'The unit states that to fulfill rights, states should take positive steps such as providing means for education, including establishing schools and hiring teachers.', 19),('3a2d0178-5131-4b70-896c-741d93c0dfb7'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Universality of human rights means all cultures must apply identical standards and practices.', 'False', 'The text states universality means rights apply equally to all people and is not synonymous with uniformity; societies may adopt higher or more specific standards.', 20),('5e3a54ba-c75b-4e2d-815e-544549ce1e93'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Second generation rights include economic, social, and cultural rights and are conceived more in positive terms that encourage state intervention.', 'True', 'The text explains that second generation rights broaden to economic, social, and cultural rights and are conceived in positive terms, encouraging state action.', 21),('795fcc44-235d-4b7f-8842-0dd5e1d81a75'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The obligation to protect requires the State to shield individuals from abuses by non-State actors and ensure access to impartial legal remedies when violations are alleged.', 'True', 'According to the text, the State must protect against abuses by non-State actors and provide access to impartial remedies.', 22),('e3c60d24-0af8-4bc9-887e-57c804c9256c'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The Universal Declaration of Human Rights (1948) is not legally binding, yet many UN member states have incorporated its principles into their national constitutions.', 'True', 'The text notes the UDHR is not legally binding but has been influential, with many states incorporating its principles into constitutions.', 23),('5e4500d5-b3ad-498b-8cd8-3b36ab437b0c'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'According to the text (UDHR Article 2), what is the only criterion someone must fulfill to enjoy human rights?', 'Being a human being.', 'The text states that human rights belong to every human being without distinction and that the only criterion to enjoy these rights is being a human.', 24),('d82588c0-8544-47e0-8fd0-642861c62c27'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'When, in principle, do individuals stop enjoying their human rights?', 'At the time of natural death.', 'The feature of eternality states that individuals stop enjoying their human rights only at natural death.', 25),('468f70e8-a2cf-467d-8fac-a198399e70f3'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Name one circumstance mentioned in the text under which some human rights may be suspended or restricted.', 'During a publicly declared national emergency, a government may impose a curfew restricting freedom of movement.', 'The text notes that in particular circumstances, such as a declared national emergency, some rights may be derogated, e.g., by imposing a curfew.', 26),('200a0668-bcd4-48f5-845f-e355a888dc86'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What does it mean that human rights are “indivisible and interdependent”?', 'Rights are intrinsically connected; enjoyment of one depends on others, and no right is more important than the rest.', 'The text explains that human rights cannot be viewed in isolation and that full enjoyment of any right depends on many others.', 27),('84377f57-8564-4e28-80b0-e6180c2d5a2a'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In the FDRE Constitution, which articles are designated “Human Rights,” and which are “Democratic Rights”?', 'Articles 14–28 are “Human Rights”; Articles 29–44 are “Democratic Rights.”', 'Chapter three divides Fundamental Rights and Freedoms into Human Rights (Arts. 14–28) and Democratic Rights (Arts. 29–44).', 28),('5dc304b6-acb5-4d62-884a-0f5a91f977b5'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Give one constitutional obligation of citizens mentioned for protecting human rights.', 'Respect for religious equality.', 'The text lists citizen obligations including respect for religious equality, gender equality, others’ rights, and the national flag.', 29),('b906a286-44ba-47c0-81b2-fdfcb5ef7df3'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'List the three types of state obligations toward human rights identified in the text.', 'Obligations to respect, to protect, and to fulfill.', 'The lesson outlines that states must respect, protect, and fulfill human rights, each with distinct duties.', 30),('c85c137f-027a-49a4-8975-974adcab3f45'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What is the legal status of the 1948 Universal Declaration of Human Rights and for what purpose was it adopted?', 'It is not legally binding; it was adopted to define the “human rights” and “fundamental freedoms” referenced in UN Charter Article 55(c).', 'The text states the UDHR is not legally binding but was adopted to define rights and freedoms that UN members must observe and respect.', 31),('11eba3e7-9672-46eb-83d7-98ec000ebbad'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many basic features of human rights are explicitly listed (Universalism, Eternality, Inalienability, Indivisible and interdependent, Inviolability, and that human rights are irrevocable)?', '6 features', 'The text names six features: Universalism; Eternality; Inalienability; Indivisible and interdependent; Inviolability; and that human rights are irrevocable. Counting them gives 6 features.', 32),('931bac86-60d9-4c69-88b1-4d02ef7e5602'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many generations of human rights are described in the lesson (first, second, and third generation rights)?', '3 generations', 'The lesson explicitly discusses three generations: first generation rights, second generation rights, and third generation rights. Counting these gives 3 generations.', 33),('4627e545-4f35-482a-8fd8-f4bded859fd0'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Articles 13–44 of the FDRE Constitution are devoted to “Fundamental Rights and Freedoms.” How many articles does this inclusive range contain?', '32 articles', 'Inclusive count: 44 − 13 + 1 = 32 articles.', 34),('36644b75-5967-469f-87d6-13c827738e42'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many articles are named “Human Rights” in the FDRE Constitution (Articles 14–28 inclusive)?', '15 articles', 'Inclusive count: 28 − 14 + 1 = 15 articles.', 35),('9dd1a0e9-fdbb-4c42-8c70-edd5ca476fc8'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many articles are dubbed “Democratic Rights” in the FDRE Constitution (Articles 29–44 inclusive)?', '16 articles', 'Inclusive count: 44 − 29 + 1 = 16 articles.', 36),('a163564b-34ef-4be7-8992-6694d541b2e8'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Across the UDHR article ranges cited for first (Articles 2–21) and second (Articles 22–27) generation rights, how many UDHR articles are covered in total?', '26 articles', 'First range count: 21 − 2 + 1 = 20 articles. Second range count: 27 − 22 + 1 = 6 articles. Total: 20 + 6 = 26 articles.', 37),('36c61580-271c-42d7-8056-1cd6577ce278'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many distinct types of state obligations to realize human rights are identified (obligation to respect, protect, and fulfill)?', '3 obligations', 'The text lists three obligations: obligation to respect; obligation to protect; obligation to fulfill. Counting them gives 3 obligations.', 38),('7d9fb8f4-6ea0-4973-8f68-09a1aeee73f5'::uuid, 'a0161ca2-b28d-4f26-8a75-71b6f6e7fd8d'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Under the obligation to fulfill the right to education, how many distinct education-related provisions are listed (free and compulsory primary education for all; free secondary education; higher education; vocational training; adult education; elimination of illiteracy)?', '6 items', 'Enumerated provisions: (1) free and compulsory primary education for all; (2) free secondary education; (3) higher education; (4) vocational training; (5) adult education; (6) elimination of illiteracy. Count = 6 items.', 39) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET quiz_id = EXCLUDED.quiz_id, question_type = EXCLUDED.question_type, question_text = EXCLUDED.question_text, correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
INSERT INTO public.choices (id, question_id, choice_text, is_correct, order_index) VALUES ('d71267d5-c9a7-4065-81d1-d21e588f68c6'::uuid, 'e4999611-7290-4b5e-88be-df5478d0b308'::uuid, 'They are legal benefits granted to citizens by their governments.', FALSE, 0),('870707ff-75dc-4ed0-82ca-a25019754219'::uuid, 'e4999611-7290-4b5e-88be-df5478d0b308'::uuid, 'They are fundamental entitlements that belong to every person simply for being human.', TRUE, 1),('86059e9a-319a-4e4a-8ce8-5a093a66e79e'::uuid, 'e4999611-7290-4b5e-88be-df5478d0b308'::uuid, 'They are privileges earned through participation in elections.', FALSE, 2),('60f188f8-141a-4d4a-83f5-61184dbf086c'::uuid, 'e4999611-7290-4b5e-88be-df5478d0b308'::uuid, 'They are rewards for obeying national laws.', FALSE, 3),('ba5eb264-a07b-44f2-8b52-89b119038960'::uuid, 'f7fa04bd-693b-45ab-8fd9-ab2d29605772'::uuid, 'A guarantee of identical lifestyles for all people', FALSE, 0),('60da18bf-1675-49ea-8974-1547bfdc9c57'::uuid, 'f7fa04bd-693b-45ab-8fd9-ab2d29605772'::uuid, 'Free public services to all citizens', FALSE, 1),('faf2f344-b0a3-45a9-85c1-84b927677a57'::uuid, 'f7fa04bd-693b-45ab-8fd9-ab2d29605772'::uuid, 'Minimum standards indispensable for a worth-living life', TRUE, 2),('611fbbde-4f5d-4ad8-8a88-2b653ad490c9'::uuid, 'f7fa04bd-693b-45ab-8fd9-ab2d29605772'::uuid, 'Maximum social equality regardless of context', FALSE, 3),('fe7e3651-7576-4500-8056-29df7daacbd5'::uuid, 'dcedbb73-0c93-4f83-89e4-037521f4eb4d'::uuid, 'They apply only to citizens within a country.', FALSE, 0),('3d1b2e11-ae5b-4577-8ae7-a324cebe513f'::uuid, 'dcedbb73-0c93-4f83-89e4-037521f4eb4d'::uuid, 'They apply equally to all people everywhere and are not time-limited.', TRUE, 1),('09afc75b-1d25-4788-8a82-34af49b991e0'::uuid, 'dcedbb73-0c93-4f83-89e4-037521f4eb4d'::uuid, 'They require identical cultural practices across societies.', FALSE, 2),('ab285bac-717f-47ab-81e4-d3bfdf79d961'::uuid, 'dcedbb73-0c93-4f83-89e4-037521f4eb4d'::uuid, 'They prioritize national interests over individual rights.', FALSE, 3),('723948a7-58da-46c5-8f39-1f43c54aed55'::uuid, '62709aef-3370-4e24-87c3-c3389aa85a22'::uuid, 'At natural death', TRUE, 0),('0d5e02cc-9256-43d1-8c0e-c006590e3359'::uuid, '62709aef-3370-4e24-87c3-c3389aa85a22'::uuid, 'When convicted of any crime', FALSE, 1),('d51a5c71-95e9-4ff7-8c6b-67c9ce093981'::uuid, '62709aef-3370-4e24-87c3-c3389aa85a22'::uuid, 'During times of national emergency', FALSE, 2),('7daf2038-7b83-4867-8d31-a88ea7e9a907'::uuid, '62709aef-3370-4e24-87c3-c3389aa85a22'::uuid, 'When they move to another country', FALSE, 3),('93b455e1-3111-4933-8067-19dc6737f31d'::uuid, 'e19ff584-2a25-4ab4-8f49-baa8d3ed11ae'::uuid, 'They can be permanently taken away by the state during emergencies.', FALSE, 0),('a6a9c4a6-37a6-427f-8a24-785bf94ab71c'::uuid, 'e19ff584-2a25-4ab4-8f49-baa8d3ed11ae'::uuid, 'They are inherent to human existence, though some may be lawfully restricted in specific circumstances.', TRUE, 1),('6d29b207-5daf-4389-84e5-6206986c3758'::uuid, 'e19ff584-2a25-4ab4-8f49-baa8d3ed11ae'::uuid, 'They apply only if a person has not committed a crime.', FALSE, 2),('a31f27ba-0465-483f-865d-9d652ae12113'::uuid, 'e19ff584-2a25-4ab4-8f49-baa8d3ed11ae'::uuid, 'They can be traded for other legal privileges.', FALSE, 3),('60bdbdfd-b681-4136-8205-bd1c58595313'::uuid, '951eecf2-3827-433b-856d-a4af60447507'::uuid, 'Economic rights can be enjoyed without civil rights.', FALSE, 0),('675e7dd3-5c05-4c61-8ca9-8047ca8026a7'::uuid, '951eecf2-3827-433b-856d-a4af60447507'::uuid, 'Rights are ranked so that some are more important than others.', FALSE, 1),('6187d904-2515-47e7-853d-2bd8eb60fdb4'::uuid, '951eecf2-3827-433b-856d-a4af60447507'::uuid, 'Progress in civil and political rights makes it easier to exercise economic, social and cultural rights.', TRUE, 2),('48424e19-62e2-4e7a-8106-e627b85dc4e7'::uuid, '951eecf2-3827-433b-856d-a4af60447507'::uuid, 'Violations of social rights do not affect other rights.', FALSE, 3),('53b46e25-355f-4b87-84de-a4de0a18d661'::uuid, '0f5fad86-8c36-4739-8476-8c4ee7193381'::uuid, 'They may be routinely limited by private actors.', FALSE, 0),('418f1179-6748-4ed6-8bd8-7da6f0820567'::uuid, '0f5fad86-8c36-4739-8476-8c4ee7193381'::uuid, 'They are expected not to be violated or even restricted by anyone.', TRUE, 1),('d1a485f4-8e24-4419-86f9-898ead975d1f'::uuid, '0f5fad86-8c36-4739-8476-8c4ee7193381'::uuid, 'They can be overridden to promote cultural uniformity.', FALSE, 2),('d023a549-5f40-42c5-87e2-329360be5548'::uuid, '0f5fad86-8c36-4739-8476-8c4ee7193381'::uuid, 'They apply only in stable times, not during crises.', FALSE, 3),('020ca800-29a2-486f-8795-177a214f2f02'::uuid, '204e3a97-89ab-4a21-87c1-489d0871f5a4'::uuid, 'They can be repealed by majority vote.', FALSE, 0),('f9294cdd-8762-4e88-8d1d-b465c7a86676'::uuid, '204e3a97-89ab-4a21-87c1-489d0871f5a4'::uuid, 'They cannot be taken away by any power or authority.', TRUE, 1),('7b72b277-07db-42f2-882f-c2bec5fb1225'::uuid, '204e3a97-89ab-4a21-87c1-489d0871f5a4'::uuid, 'They are temporary privileges during emergencies.', FALSE, 2),('af6e4b5e-fc19-44ea-8943-c482ee4bef5f'::uuid, '204e3a97-89ab-4a21-87c1-489d0871f5a4'::uuid, 'They are negotiable based on social status.', FALSE, 3),('bde12a87-932a-42c7-8572-707ff720db66'::uuid, 'ebb1e294-51dd-46ad-8076-d5b62b4812f6'::uuid, 'Right to social security', FALSE, 0),('32bda078-64b1-4428-863a-bf3d41df0bba'::uuid, 'ebb1e294-51dd-46ad-8076-d5b62b4812f6'::uuid, 'Freedom from torture and from cruel, inhuman, or degrading treatment', TRUE, 1),('0f68eb23-6eaa-467f-8e37-d69ff2e9f9e7'::uuid, 'ebb1e294-51dd-46ad-8076-d5b62b4812f6'::uuid, 'Right to education', FALSE, 2),('f8f5f81a-5215-4812-8fb6-de0c53e9d425'::uuid, 'ebb1e294-51dd-46ad-8076-d5b62b4812f6'::uuid, 'Right to economic and social development', FALSE, 3),('71c8094c-c90c-4857-82f3-0aafec6c53a2'::uuid, 'd1e0bb62-237e-4d73-8758-13839d203187'::uuid, 'Freedom from arbitrary arrest and detention', FALSE, 0),('4dce9ee8-4f36-4354-831f-3ab2d4a1766d'::uuid, 'd1e0bb62-237e-4d73-8758-13839d203187'::uuid, 'Right to participate in government through free elections', FALSE, 1),('1d542a02-9ce8-4e9a-85b9-22c5d2e9d7c3'::uuid, 'd1e0bb62-237e-4d73-8758-13839d203187'::uuid, 'Right to work', TRUE, 2),('6cd68790-d1a9-404f-8b93-3762d99f24e7'::uuid, 'd1e0bb62-237e-4d73-8758-13839d203187'::uuid, 'Freedom of opinion and expression', FALSE, 3),('16b80dc3-85f1-40d2-87f4-7cebddb53ce3'::uuid, '1c829af1-dd28-4c24-8c64-f95d721622ea'::uuid, 'Right to a fair and public trial', FALSE, 0),('4c2aafbd-9d8e-4ab6-8a96-3119cef46bec'::uuid, '1c829af1-dd28-4c24-8c64-f95d721622ea'::uuid, 'Right to political, economic, social, and cultural self-determination', TRUE, 1),('a794acff-325f-4f23-8764-a49664c8ef11'::uuid, '1c829af1-dd28-4c24-8c64-f95d721622ea'::uuid, 'Freedom from slavery', FALSE, 2),('9450e44f-5229-42cb-8b1e-f72306d4b24a'::uuid, '1c829af1-dd28-4c24-8c64-f95d721622ea'::uuid, 'Right to a standard of living adequate for health and well-being', FALSE, 3),('9dbfbcc9-59e4-407d-8bbb-b9da2297978d'::uuid, '87e49887-cff8-46b0-8f5a-a7402505caf9'::uuid, 'Universality requires uniform cultural practices.', FALSE, 0),('69a5d657-c80e-483e-8c83-150aa5039690'::uuid, '87e49887-cff8-46b0-8f5a-a7402505caf9'::uuid, 'Universality does not threaten diversity and allows states to define higher standards.', TRUE, 1),('c3a64040-f339-4b9e-85b2-b8d20c225e9b'::uuid, '87e49887-cff8-46b0-8f5a-a7402505caf9'::uuid, 'Diversity is incompatible with equal human rights.', FALSE, 2),('729c7218-9eca-48cc-8c4c-89006f87ff99'::uuid, '87e49887-cff8-46b0-8f5a-a7402505caf9'::uuid, 'Universalism applies only to civil rights, not social rights.', FALSE, 3),('0bb9790c-0ccb-4092-85df-0c450c8693a1'::uuid, '0253e3c7-e231-4460-8c1f-3933187bbbfd'::uuid, 'Human rights are granted by government discretion.', FALSE, 0),('db726ccd-c3d5-424d-8c71-677956a528b4'::uuid, '0253e3c7-e231-4460-8c1f-3933187bbbfd'::uuid, 'Human rights and freedoms, emanating from the nature of mankind, are inviolable and inalienable.', TRUE, 1),('9c78d63f-8090-48f0-8247-5050d842e1c7'::uuid, '0253e3c7-e231-4460-8c1f-3933187bbbfd'::uuid, 'Only democratic rights are justiciable in courts.', FALSE, 2),('912150ec-ae6d-44eb-8e12-e55ec9ff5387'::uuid, '0253e3c7-e231-4460-8c1f-3933187bbbfd'::uuid, 'Human rights apply only to citizens.', FALSE, 3),('9abb4104-d21c-426b-8c1f-796fb83723e1'::uuid, 'e26e55be-f858-4efe-8c2d-08629dc490fe'::uuid, 'Articles 1–10', FALSE, 0),('d90237eb-8599-4fb1-8ca0-4cacd62271ee'::uuid, 'e26e55be-f858-4efe-8c2d-08629dc490fe'::uuid, 'Articles 14–28', TRUE, 1),('527ca008-8d96-4c21-8cb6-b882223b00a9'::uuid, 'e26e55be-f858-4efe-8c2d-08629dc490fe'::uuid, 'Articles 29–44', FALSE, 2),('5141b5af-d84d-4a55-8b6b-e47f7b59726b'::uuid, 'e26e55be-f858-4efe-8c2d-08629dc490fe'::uuid, 'Articles 2–21', FALSE, 3),('7599f831-9d7a-471a-8698-264b134f3b82'::uuid, '7e9a6593-82fb-40ad-8e32-1feca5c5e3a4'::uuid, 'Inviolable and inalienable', TRUE, 0),('08179220-7d51-4c43-8aa4-2835fd969cc6'::uuid, '7e9a6593-82fb-40ad-8e32-1feca5c5e3a4'::uuid, 'Temporary and transferable', FALSE, 1),('0e2cf514-ee95-4be1-8830-aaf900b704e6'::uuid, '7e9a6593-82fb-40ad-8e32-1feca5c5e3a4'::uuid, 'Limited to elected representatives', FALSE, 2),('9f376f2f-c40c-45d8-8716-f41f0dd4e198'::uuid, '7e9a6593-82fb-40ad-8e32-1feca5c5e3a4'::uuid, 'Available only during emergencies', FALSE, 3),('1fe5ded9-7fae-4bc4-8c5f-91ecfd9cffa4'::uuid, 'd7f90740-7c1b-45fa-8f5f-977d41553de4'::uuid, 'Support only the majority’s views', FALSE, 0),('0d363adc-ba49-4d88-8f8e-8c0f21e2b746'::uuid, 'd7f90740-7c1b-45fa-8f5f-977d41553de4'::uuid, 'Respect for religious equality', TRUE, 1),('2ce999a2-10d2-4776-876f-24232db8256e'::uuid, 'd7f90740-7c1b-45fa-8f5f-977d41553de4'::uuid, 'Censor opposing opinions', FALSE, 2),('19e057a9-6d53-4474-8ac4-f549149cd20d'::uuid, 'd7f90740-7c1b-45fa-8f5f-977d41553de4'::uuid, 'Avoid participation in public affairs', FALSE, 3),('14b9f33b-7434-4dbe-845e-58d05bcc5ce5'::uuid, '82414da8-8d0f-4f73-88c3-1e62a4dce9fc'::uuid, 'Without considering others’ rights', FALSE, 0),('549caa22-a4a9-4a90-82fa-5193d8389e9b'::uuid, '82414da8-8d0f-4f73-88c3-1e62a4dce9fc'::uuid, 'Only when approved by private actors', FALSE, 1),('0d63a689-fa26-4fb8-8d1a-578eb59adf10'::uuid, '82414da8-8d0f-4f73-88c3-1e62a4dce9fc'::uuid, 'With due regard for the rights of others', TRUE, 2),('e4b32947-5acd-4dff-8569-52914283c281'::uuid, '82414da8-8d0f-4f73-88c3-1e62a4dce9fc'::uuid, 'Only in private settings', FALSE, 3),('660f1e20-f0f5-444b-8223-fe52ac442377'::uuid, '74f18bce-efae-4349-89d3-7a8ed87c25d5'::uuid, 'Enacting laws against human rights abuses by private actors', FALSE, 0),('b1854c1c-5f33-4d77-8212-ea43e8005ab5'::uuid, '74f18bce-efae-4349-89d3-7a8ed87c25d5'::uuid, 'Performing medical experiments on persons with disabilities without their consent', TRUE, 1),('ee7b1e69-8ad9-44c9-8a60-86d02f867949'::uuid, '74f18bce-efae-4349-89d3-7a8ed87c25d5'::uuid, 'Providing impartial legal remedies for violations', FALSE, 2),('2a369579-e3d4-43d6-89e7-330d794f6ea6'::uuid, '74f18bce-efae-4349-89d3-7a8ed87c25d5'::uuid, 'Hiring more teachers to expand access to education', FALSE, 3),('c9f873cf-93b5-4f2c-8868-ddac336de0c3'::uuid, '80c1fa83-1405-413b-8278-d8f9dab995dd'::uuid, 'Restricting all civil liberties during emergencies', FALSE, 0),('dbb3fb02-0554-49a0-8603-a08c85dcb3eb'::uuid, '80c1fa83-1405-413b-8278-d8f9dab995dd'::uuid, 'Acting against abuses by non-state actors and ensuring access to remedies', TRUE, 1),('e4808609-6eb2-41f1-8f94-600a760a883b'::uuid, '80c1fa83-1405-413b-8278-d8f9dab995dd'::uuid, 'Leaving rights enforcement to families and private groups', FALSE, 2),('4b9855ae-12ea-4307-8ddf-c5d75c312ef6'::uuid, '80c1fa83-1405-413b-8278-d8f9dab995dd'::uuid, 'Focusing only on criminal law enforcement', FALSE, 3),('9d87cf60-5629-404d-87bb-553b28f68438'::uuid, 'a62961bc-8c5f-4701-8cf1-092a8561c6bc'::uuid, 'Reducing public schools to encourage private providers', FALSE, 0),('80488713-febe-42f6-8140-f9e0ee855a13'::uuid, 'a62961bc-8c5f-4701-8cf1-092a8561c6bc'::uuid, 'Setting up enough public schools or hiring and remunerating adequate numbers of teachers', TRUE, 1),('340f4403-7167-45c5-8bbe-149d416267db'::uuid, 'a62961bc-8c5f-4701-8cf1-092a8561c6bc'::uuid, 'Allowing third parties to indoctrinate students', FALSE, 2),('16e6c413-5340-4099-816d-5e7a9a1490b7'::uuid, 'a62961bc-8c5f-4701-8cf1-092a8561c6bc'::uuid, 'Excluding persons with disabilities from school on cost grounds', FALSE, 3),('60b2254c-5fd6-4d3a-84c4-8fd7e26046fc'::uuid, '3a2d0178-5131-4b70-896c-741d93c0dfb7'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('208bce1f-79cb-4101-868c-68f48506ef9d'::uuid, '3a2d0178-5131-4b70-896c-741d93c0dfb7'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1),('31cd5420-9029-43d4-867a-9743f55ccf55'::uuid, '5e3a54ba-c75b-4e2d-815e-544549ce1e93'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('5e1d6df3-0a61-41db-8fdc-648433507a9c'::uuid, '5e3a54ba-c75b-4e2d-815e-544549ce1e93'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('b4be4a8b-c8d3-42d4-8784-5a4c1a0235e8'::uuid, '795fcc44-235d-4b7f-8842-0dd5e1d81a75'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('a3a9b4fb-fee0-42cd-8df8-085f09d21e84'::uuid, '795fcc44-235d-4b7f-8842-0dd5e1d81a75'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('84d8b2bc-7853-4c22-8d84-fe3d1a6fe55a'::uuid, 'e3c60d24-0af8-4bc9-887e-57c804c9256c'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('5fb170b2-881e-4097-8fc4-693f8e93646c'::uuid, 'e3c60d24-0af8-4bc9-887e-57c804c9256c'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question_id = EXCLUDED.question_id, choice_text = EXCLUDED.choice_text, is_correct = EXCLUDED.is_correct, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
INSERT INTO public.quizzes (id, subject, unit, title, description) VALUES ('a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'Citizenship', 'Unit 7', 'Molarum Grade 10 — Citizenship Unit 7: Patriotism', 'Source-grounded Molarum Grade 10 Citizenship questions for Unit 7: Patriotism.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET subject = EXCLUDED.subject, unit = EXCLUDED.unit, title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, quiz_id, question_type, question_text, correct_answer, explanation, order_index) VALUES ('519f6b9d-605d-47a5-883d-4eb9262ecfa9'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'From which Latin term does the word ''patriotism'' originate according to the text?', 'patria', 'The excerpt states that patriotism has originated from the Latin term ''patria'', which means father land.', 0),('d4ce1b8d-edd2-4c3a-8f81-3a841dfc77ec'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which wording from the excerpt best defines patriotism?', 'A sentiment; a psychological attachment to one’s nation', 'The text explicitly defines patriotism as ''a sentiment; a psychological attachment to one’s nation.''', 1),('d04055ae-8ade-4595-8322-fb80853e7d96'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the excerpt, which of the following is part of patriotism in a democratic system?', 'Devoting time, ability, knowledge and even life for fundamental principles', 'The excerpt states that in a democratic system patriotism means devoting time, ability, knowledge and even life for the fundamental principles on which the nation’s security and welfare depend.', 2),('f4a116ee-9a87-45c6-8aeb-205a8f5a80eb'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following is listed as a type of patriotism in the excerpt?', 'Icon patriotism', 'The excerpt lists Icon patriotism among the types of patriotism, while the other choices are not listed in the unit''s types.', 3),('6e395817-3ca6-4587-8ad8-75fe06ea64d7'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Constitutional patriotism, as described in the text, most directly emphasizes:', 'Commitment to democracy and human rights', 'The excerpt defines constitutional patriotism as a strong commitment or alignment with democracy and human rights and devotion to fundamental values and principles.', 4),('595c3d4f-e0b1-4da4-8da3-cdd78b5a23d6'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which feature characterizes traditional patriotism in the excerpt?', 'Readiness to give one’s life for the mother land', 'The text states that traditional patriotism refers to someone''s readiness to give his or her life for the mother land and that it does not attempt to align feelings with democratic principles.', 5),('c1a2ca65-763a-4626-87b4-b3d43481485d'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the text, an ''icon patriot'' is someone who:', 'Shows love for the country through actions and may risk their life to defend it', 'The excerpt explains that icon patriots show love for the country through actions that have positive impact and are even willing to risk their lives to defend their homeland.', 6),('01c3cc7b-9c58-47f9-83bc-ba827c3277b4'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which action is given in the excerpt as an example of symbolic patriotism?', 'Respect for national symbols such as the flag and national anthem', 'Symbolic patriotism is described in the text as respect for national symbols, including the flag and national anthem, which can evoke patriotic spirit.', 7),('4152d797-ce19-4dd5-8f5b-a9270c6d2fde'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following best illustrates ''capital patriotism'' as defined in the excerpt?', 'Contributing to the national economy and development', 'The book explains capital patriotism as actions of individuals who focus on development of the national economy and contributing to society''s well-being.', 8),('599ba2af-c5b7-4f28-89df-6aaf23877f1b'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the unit, environmental patriotism primarily involves:', 'Showing love for the country’s environment through protection and improvement', 'The excerpt states that environmental patriotism refers to feelings of love for the country’s environment and actions made to improve quality of life and the environment.', 9),('935fc342-5a6b-4c88-883a-7dcc4850a2f4'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which principle is identified as a basis of constitutional patriotism in the excerpt?', 'Equality', 'The text explains that constitutional patriotism is based upon the principle of equality, respecting democratic rights and human rights as in the constitution.', 10),('6b1e1b94-ea81-4444-86bd-a1d9e7a4d231'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Why is tolerance described as important for true patriotism in the excerpt?', 'Because it allows diverse groups to have common ground and peaceful coexistence', 'The excerpt states tolerance is important so different ethnic groups can have common ground, mutual understanding, and peaceful resolution of conflicts.', 11),('8660e3b0-4c89-411e-8d2e-6cffad41c7d9'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the excerpt, constitutional loyalty expects citizens to be loyal to:', 'Their constitution, the people, elected government and community', 'The excerpt specifies that constitutional patriotism is based upon loyalty to the constitution, to the people, to their elected government and to the community at large.', 12),('27a75971-393d-4562-88b3-6d2e7546a3ff'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which statement matches the excerpt about personal sacrifice for patriotism?', 'True patriots sacrifice personal desires and interests for the common good', 'The excerpt directly states that true patriots sacrifice personal desires and interests for the common good as part of patriotic basis.', 13),('885637b4-8bb7-4345-871a-cc4f37ef4733'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What does the excerpt say about the constitution?', 'Any law or decision contravening the constitution shall be of no effect', 'The text states the constitution is the supreme law and that any law, customary practice or decision contravening it shall be of no effect.', 14),('b49d0681-5ba6-4205-8bb9-8278606460e6'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which behavior is given as an example of a patriotic trait in the case study about Roza?', 'Refusing to accept a bribe and giving fair treatment to patients', 'The case study asks whether Roza should accept 500 Birr to give unfair favor and implies that rejecting such an offer and acting ethically is a patriotic trait.', 15),('dc6befe5-a12a-41f4-8423-b675cc93cb87'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following is mentioned in the excerpt as a way to promote the common good?', 'Keeping state secrets that endanger the nation and working together on common problems', 'The text explains promoting the common good includes keeping state secrets whose exposure would endanger the nation and joint effort on common problems.', 16),('3421569e-9729-4da4-809d-0172cf6b0503'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which factor listed in the excerpt works against the common good?', 'Corruption', 'The excerpt identifies corruption, including nepotism and embezzlement, as damaging to the common good and eroding trust and civic virtue.', 17),('5882eef5-e71e-41a5-8ac3-46148be6f45f'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the excerpt, which is a way patriotism brings people together?', 'Creating a sense of unity and togetherness, for example feeling belonging when seeing the national flag', 'The text explains that patriotism brings people together by developing unity and a sense of belonging, illustrated by the example of watching the Ethiopian flag.', 18),('15f7b3ab-fcca-4b08-857f-81c6abd25650'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which trait is described in the excerpt as characteristic of patriotic citizens?', 'Awareness of their rights and duties', 'The excerpt lists awareness of rights and duties as a trait of patriotic citizens who avoid taking undue advantage and fulfill their obligations.', 19),('23fa9175-a512-48e1-880c-1afbae0030a7'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Patriotism is about love of one’s country or nation.', 'True', 'The unit introduction states that patriotism means love of one’s country or nation, describing political allegiance and commitment.', 20),('e6359e7c-b0e7-41e4-85d8-e6af56fc7fba'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The FDRE Constitution was ratified in 1994.', 'True', 'The excerpt explicitly states that the foundation for human rights observance in Ethiopia is the FDRE Constitution, which was ratified in 1994.', 21),('adaafb5e-62c7-4ea2-8bbf-4024d20ea845'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'true_false', 'According to the excerpt, the ''obligation to fulfill'' requires states to take positive action to ensure human rights can be realized.', 'True', 'The unit summary declares the realization of human rights is an obligation, and the unit review notes states must take positive action under the ''obligation to fulfill''.', 22),('cfbe6e0b-b083-4387-8708-47ec4bdaf056'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Traditional patriotism aligns one’s feelings with democratic principles.', 'False', 'The excerpt explains that traditional patriotism celebrates particularistic belonging and makes no attempt to align one’s feelings with democratic principles.', 23),('2fc12bb2-bcbd-4cf4-803b-0c5259f43c84'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Briefly define ''patriotism'' as given in the unit.', 'A sentiment or psychological attachment to one’s nation, meaning love of one’s country or homeland.', 'The excerpt defines patriotism as a sentiment and psychological attachment to one’s nation, originating from ''patria'' meaning father land and involving love and devotion to the country.', 24),('17936f65-8605-48e2-855f-faf7eb89cbc0'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'List four types of patriotism named in the excerpt.', 'Constitutional patriotism, Traditional patriotism, Icon patriotism, Symbolic patriotism.', 'The unit lists multiple types including constitutional, traditional, icon and symbolic patriotism among others such as capital and environmental patriotism.', 25),('6cb5b998-b9b7-4346-84d6-0c08a4ce6111'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What does constitutional patriotism imply about coexistence and difference?', 'It implies coexistence, mutual understanding, tolerance, and peaceful resolution of conflicts while appreciating people with different languages, colors, sex and religion.', 'The excerpt says constitutional patriotism includes acknowledgment and appreciation of people with different characteristics and promotes coexistence, tolerance and peaceful conflict resolution.', 26),('2edbdc98-63e5-44df-84f4-f05fa0385674'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Give two national symbols mentioned that evoke symbolic patriotism.', 'The flag and the national anthem.', 'The excerpt lists the flag and the national anthem as national symbols whose use can evoke patriotic spirit as examples of symbolic patriotism.', 27),('95e0971a-62da-4ddc-809d-ac2e827c900f'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Why is tolerance described as a constitutional and civil obligation in Ethiopia today?', 'Because the democratic system recognizes differences and multiculturalism, requiring citizens to respect and accept differences for peaceful coexistence.', 'The excerpt explains that in the current democratic and constitutional system, tolerance is not a gift but a constitutional and civil obligation to respect and accept differences for peaceful co-existence.', 28),('6a363faa-c6ba-4b9f-8498-269b923a474d'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'According to the excerpt, what should patriots do when exposed to state secrets that endanger the nation?', 'They should keep such state secrets and not communicate them to a third party.', 'The text indicates that information whose exposure endangers the nation must be kept secret and not communicated to third parties to promote the common good.', 29),('80215398-56c4-48a3-84e2-5b2511c5fbab'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In the Roza case study, how is Roza evaluated if she refuses the offered 500 Birr to give unfair favour?', 'She is evaluated as exhibiting patriotic traits by acting ethically and not taking undue advantage for personal gain.', 'The case study implies that refusing the offer and treating patients fairly demonstrates patriotic traits such as not taking undue advantage and serving the common good.', 30),('862e9a1a-c420-4913-8984-5a78c667533c'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide adopted as listed in the excerpt?', '1948', 'The excerpt lists the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide with the year (1948).', 31),('59ae89ad-6835-47af-8687-cb80898df46b'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was the Convention Relating to the Status of Refugees adopted as shown in the excerpt?', '1951', 'The excerpt lists the Convention Relating to the Status of Refugees with the year (1951).', 32),('469ed386-d4fe-404f-8095-3aae39f05c23'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'According to the excerpt, in what year was the Slavery Convention originally adopted?', '1926', 'The excerpt shows the Slavery Convention with the year (1926) and notes it was later amended by Protocol in 1953.', 33),('a21d2c27-873c-417d-839a-d03ac2f34947'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was the Slavery Convention amended by Protocol according to the excerpt?', '1953', 'The excerpt indicates the Slavery Convention was amended by Protocol in 1953.', 34),('c9c6bf3f-62a5-4cab-8284-3dfaa60f87fb'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year were the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights and the International Covenant on Economic, Social and Cultural Rights listed as adopted in the excerpt?', '1966', 'The excerpt lists both the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights and the International Covenant on Economic, Social and Cultural Rights with the year (1966).', 35),('de8b9ed5-c3a8-45a4-8526-02f3e3c7dec9'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'In what year was the FDRE Constitution ratified, according to the excerpt?', '1994', 'The excerpt clearly states that the FDRE Constitution was ratified in 1994 and is the supreme law of the land.', 36),('c46f3534-ddf7-4cae-886e-84ab28c4f315'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'The magazine ''L’illustrazioneItaliana'' used an illustration on May 29 of which year to describe the victory at Adwa as given in the excerpt?', '1896', 'The excerpt mentions that the illustration was used by ''L’illustrazioneItaliana'' magazine on May 29,1896 to describe the victory of Ethiopia at Adwa.', 37),('746bd6e5-7bf9-41d9-8093-608464d9e3aa'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'According to the caption in the excerpt, on what date did the Battle of Adwa occur as listed (day, month, year)? Provide the year only as a number.', '1996', 'The figure caption in the excerpt states the battle occurred on March 1, 1996 as printed in the text.', 38),('02a4a8b4-0401-4470-8bbc-fbc4010ad21f'::uuid, 'a9442f07-c4fc-4725-8760-f25ec6e5251e'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Name two ways the excerpt says patriotism is important for a nation.', 'Bringing people together to create unity and motivating citizens to work for the betterment of the country.', 'The excerpt explains patriotism brings people together by creating unity and also motivates individuals to work towards national improvement and support one another.', 39) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET quiz_id = EXCLUDED.quiz_id, question_type = EXCLUDED.question_type, question_text = EXCLUDED.question_text, correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
