lecting national symbols', FALSE, 2),('2b60dd69-7184-44bb-888e-37028fccfef7'::uuid, 'c1a2ca65-763a-4626-87b4-b3d43481485d'::uuid, 'Avoids public service to preserve personal comfort', FALSE, 3),('268df215-4de0-48b0-8706-fea32b036249'::uuid, '01c3cc7b-9c58-47f9-83bc-ba827c3277b4'::uuid, 'Respect for national symbols such as the flag and national anthem', TRUE, 0),('8e31eefc-d9a1-47c0-8062-a7d64895a165'::uuid, '01c3cc7b-9c58-47f9-83bc-ba827c3277b4'::uuid, 'Donating to foreign charities only', FALSE, 1),('f4982d15-4c09-43e5-8cf2-f2b9dfa58376'::uuid, '01c3cc7b-9c58-47f9-83bc-ba827c3277b4'::uuid, 'Working solely for personal profit', FALSE, 2),('1508f49f-bff3-430f-8de9-bf36107c763c'::uuid, '01c3cc7b-9c58-47f9-83bc-ba827c3277b4'::uuid, 'Undermining national symbols to protest', FALSE, 3),('4c0b8bf0-d177-4ca7-83bb-7a3704cf8025'::uuid, '4152d797-ce19-4dd5-8f5b-a9270c6d2fde'::uuid, 'Contributing to the national economy and development', TRUE, 0),('e0088eb7-b080-472f-85fd-db8d9ccd33fe'::uuid, '4152d797-ce19-4dd5-8f5b-a9270c6d2fde'::uuid, 'Leading military parades only', FALSE, 1),('ef989b6e-1e48-4317-8a35-9603cffc6f54'::uuid, '4152d797-ce19-4dd5-8f5b-a9270c6d2fde'::uuid, 'Displaying historical artifacts without civic engagement', FALSE, 2),('ca236526-3130-4a18-865d-fd076de8bbfd'::uuid, '4152d797-ce19-4dd5-8f5b-a9270c6d2fde'::uuid, 'Ignoring economic issues to focus on symbols', FALSE, 3),('266bc13b-8018-4305-8224-0fff8ad9553a'::uuid, '599ba2af-c5b7-4f28-89df-6aaf23877f1b'::uuid, 'Showing love for the country’s environment through protection and improvement', TRUE, 0),('0adb5457-610c-4f51-876f-e882cb911fb1'::uuid, '599ba2af-c5b7-4f28-89df-6aaf23877f1b'::uuid, 'Focusing only on urban development projects', FALSE, 1),('d12eaf52-7906-47e1-85af-4bbb71de621d'::uuid, '599ba2af-c5b7-4f28-89df-6aaf23877f1b'::uuid, 'Exporting natural resources regardless of local impact', FALSE, 2),('98acc47c-bd95-4f80-8a97-90d585ad32b7'::uuid, '599ba2af-c5b7-4f28-89df-6aaf23877f1b'::uuid, 'Privatizing community green spaces', FALSE, 3),('6b0a8508-f6b8-4f66-8828-7205c270af78'::uuid, '935fc342-5a6b-4c88-883a-7dcc4850a2f4'::uuid, 'Equality', TRUE, 0),('fc06bd10-2701-49ad-8fe3-b1044fe69a07'::uuid, '935fc342-5a6b-4c88-883a-7dcc4850a2f4'::uuid, 'Ethnic supremacy', FALSE, 1),('ef7d21e0-82ff-45d6-8fb6-ed4a84685612'::uuid, '935fc342-5a6b-4c88-883a-7dcc4850a2f4'::uuid, 'Absolute conformity to rulers', FALSE, 2),('536fb184-1ba3-401a-8cf7-c886298af269'::uuid, '935fc342-5a6b-4c88-883a-7dcc4850a2f4'::uuid, 'Isolationism', FALSE, 3),('b93ae6d6-cad5-4025-8fc7-d40b047c8156'::uuid, '6b1e1b94-ea81-4444-86bd-a1d9e7a4d231'::uuid, 'Because it allows diverse groups to have common ground and peaceful coexistence', TRUE, 0),('d0331eb9-c486-43ff-8264-0886ac912441'::uuid, '6b1e1b94-ea81-4444-86bd-a1d9e7a4d231'::uuid, 'Because it requires suppression of cultural differences', FALSE, 1),('f5ce4f09-9d01-49eb-83b6-aa89710e2d88'::uuid, '6b1e1b94-ea81-4444-86bd-a1d9e7a4d231'::uuid, 'Because it mandates a single national culture', FALSE, 2),('532e0798-d40a-47e8-8fb4-703be0c8820a'::uuid, '6b1e1b94-ea81-4444-86bd-a1d9e7a4d231'::uuid, 'Because it discourages participation in democratic processes', FALSE, 3),('4e650bf7-eaf4-4bd6-8175-a08165d1756a'::uuid, '8660e3b0-4c89-411e-8d2e-6cffad41c7d9'::uuid, 'Their constitution, the people, elected government and community', TRUE, 0),('7a8b887b-4838-4e75-8601-1bcffbaaa3d3'::uuid, '8660e3b0-4c89-411e-8d2e-6cffad41c7d9'::uuid, 'Only their own ethnic group', FALSE, 1),('c67446fd-2de2-4e8d-838c-033fab996542'::uuid, '8660e3b0-4c89-411e-8d2e-6cffad41c7d9'::uuid, 'Foreign governments', FALSE, 2),('f6d37fb6-2266-4f19-8535-102606c31efc'::uuid, '8660e3b0-4c89-411e-8d2e-6cffad41c7d9'::uuid, 'Private corporations', FALSE, 3),('14167858-7432-4b7d-8f81-d4f2849df4dc'::uuid, '27a75971-393d-4562-88b3-6d2e7546a3ff'::uuid, 'True patriots sacrifice personal desires and interests for the common good', TRUE, 0),('5f16e57e-5977-4e4b-86e5-6bdb0e0479da'::uuid, '27a75971-393d-4562-88b3-6d2e7546a3ff'::uuid, 'Patriots must always place personal interests above community needs', FALSE, 1),('9306477e-eec7-40a6-8608-54220207fca7'::uuid, '27a75971-393d-4562-88b3-6d2e7546a3ff'::uuid, 'Sacrifice is irrelevant to the concept of patriotism', FALSE, 2),('a1314957-4ac2-4d9d-8518-c7a5c856e87b'::uuid, '27a75971-393d-4562-88b3-6d2e7546a3ff'::uuid, 'Patriotism demands self-isolation from community problems', FALSE, 3),('1ea70959-8972-480e-8158-be97de60f742'::uuid, '885637b4-8bb7-4345-871a-cc4f37ef4733'::uuid, 'Any law or decision contravening the constitution shall be of no effect', TRUE, 0),('f692bd0e-9345-4925-8a9c-5d98eac66cc7'::uuid, '885637b4-8bb7-4345-871a-cc4f37ef4733'::uuid, 'Constitutional provisions are optional guidelines', FALSE, 1),('1155b7d7-bdd6-40a0-8f87-1614bc31c6d5'::uuid, '885637b4-8bb7-4345-871a-cc4f37ef4733'::uuid, 'Customary practices always override the constitution', FALSE, 2),('a7af13f4-c204-4dfa-8760-e0a03fad6b4a'::uuid, '885637b4-8bb7-4345-871a-cc4f37ef4733'::uuid, 'Public officials may ignore the constitution when convenient', FALSE, 3),('7957a21f-6bd1-41fb-805a-9df09a1a0eff'::uuid, 'b49d0681-5ba6-4205-8bb9-8278606460e6'::uuid, 'Refusing to accept a bribe and giving fair treatment to patients', TRUE, 0),('43c5d336-1570-4811-87b1-9e285c1c485b'::uuid, 'b49d0681-5ba6-4205-8bb9-8278606460e6'::uuid, 'Accepting money to prioritize one patient over others', FALSE, 1),('0a720808-7551-4219-8bcf-f95b3bb8bf01'::uuid, 'b49d0681-5ba6-4205-8bb9-8278606460e6'::uuid, 'Selling hospital supplies for private gain', FALSE, 2),('5f07d9a2-4df7-49ee-8855-c5e489086a55'::uuid, 'b49d0681-5ba6-4205-8bb9-8278606460e6'::uuid, 'Avoiding work when the hospital is busy', FALSE, 3),('1abdc979-3793-4aed-8056-b52fd41e81b6'::uuid, 'dc6befe5-a12a-41f4-8423-b675cc93cb87'::uuid, 'Keeping state secrets that endanger the nation and working together on common problems', TRUE, 0),('8a29b061-3bcb-4401-8ca1-deec8827ae76'::uuid, 'dc6befe5-a12a-41f4-8423-b675cc93cb87'::uuid, 'Publishing all confidential military information publicly', FALSE, 1),('726ff780-ed1b-4303-8411-42cb78cf9298'::uuid, 'dc6befe5-a12a-41f4-8423-b675cc93cb87'::uuid, 'Pursuing personal ambitions at the community''s expense', FALSE, 2),('c70b7181-ad46-4fa7-88b4-73406c4bc86b'::uuid, 'dc6befe5-a12a-41f4-8423-b675cc93cb87'::uuid, 'Engaging in corruption to benefit select individuals', FALSE, 3),('8de772df-86c1-4598-8d54-98a0eddb3d0f'::uuid, '3421569e-9729-4da4-809d-0172cf6b0503'::uuid, 'Corruption', TRUE, 0),('42455041-5d85-4070-8159-92b9e7f974f2'::uuid, '3421569e-9729-4da4-809d-0172cf6b0503'::uuid, 'Voluntarism', FALSE, 1),('ff49dfba-503d-41a8-8d43-5392f879f5be'::uuid, '3421569e-9729-4da4-809d-0172cf6b0503'::uuid, 'Tolerance', FALSE, 2),('541de68a-8c2c-4aa6-8560-73e8e214d4a6'::uuid, '3421569e-9729-4da4-809d-0172cf6b0503'::uuid, 'Carrying out civic duties', FALSE, 3),('e38d103f-aece-494a-8604-258e391624ce'::uuid, '5882eef5-e71e-41a5-8ac3-46148be6f45f'::uuid, 'Creating a sense of unity and togetherness, for example feeling belonging when seeing the national flag', TRUE, 0),('2ddb8754-7960-4846-8f11-7523eeef9283'::uuid, '5882eef5-e71e-41a5-8ac3-46148be6f45f'::uuid, 'Encouraging isolation of local communities', FALSE, 1),('e73afb7c-6927-46fd-8f00-6c518a0d75ee'::uuid, '5882eef5-e71e-41a5-8ac3-46148be6f45f'::uuid, 'Promoting competition that displaces cooperation', FALSE, 2),('d0872dd1-d853-413b-8041-c7dc921c8d47'::uuid, '5882eef5-e71e-41a5-8ac3-46148be6f45f'::uuid, 'Fostering mistrust between citizens', FALSE, 3),('8f268e8e-25ca-4426-88a1-325bd6ff85bf'::uuid, '15f7b3ab-fcca-4b08-857f-81c6abd25650'::uuid, 'Awareness of their rights and duties', TRUE, 0),('15c68c05-f970-446f-8c90-159e1768ee77'::uuid, '15f7b3ab-fcca-4b08-857f-81c6abd25650'::uuid, 'Seeking undue special benefits for themselves', FALSE, 1),('880b53e8-29ef-49af-8739-16e070641705'::uuid, '15f7b3ab-fcca-4b08-857f-81c6abd25650'::uuid, 'Avoiding responsibility for communal tasks', FALSE, 2),('10c19e4d-6bdb-4c1a-84dd-3127026a058d'::uuid, '15f7b3ab-fcca-4b08-857f-81c6abd25650'::uuid, 'Refusing to work with others', FALSE, 3),('107fd0b9-31fa-43cc-8535-888c3b120b9a'::uuid, '23fa9175-a512-48e1-880c-1afbae0030a7'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('39f29c75-9498-48bf-8b50-38cc3dc5fbef'::uuid, '23fa9175-a512-48e1-880c-1afbae0030a7'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('0c2c7868-d28b-4de6-8b29-cd4a2b9a0112'::uuid, 'e6359e7c-b0e7-41e4-85d8-e6af56fc7fba'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('4af78917-d5a7-49d6-853a-12f1ed13f22f'::uuid, 'e6359e7c-b0e7-41e4-85d8-e6af56fc7fba'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('d6330e0d-b70b-44cc-8c7b-62ac5d77f313'::uuid, 'adaafb5e-62c7-4ea2-8bbf-4024d20ea845'::uuid, 'True', TRUE, 0),('31305dde-11c2-4f3b-84c9-0fb1a7402f25'::uuid, 'adaafb5e-62c7-4ea2-8bbf-4024d20ea845'::uuid, 'False', FALSE, 1),('dcee65d9-02e6-4965-85f0-2b85f932277b'::uuid, 'cfbe6e0b-b083-4387-8708-47ec4bdaf056'::uuid, 'True', FALSE, 0),('9333dd1a-2147-4e33-816b-c9a624d3da9a'::uuid, 'cfbe6e0b-b083-4387-8708-47ec4bdaf056'::uuid, 'False', TRUE, 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question_id = EXCLUDED.question_id, choice_text = EXCLUDED.choice_text, is_correct = EXCLUDED.is_correct, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
INSERT INTO public.quizzes (id, subject, unit, title, description) VALUES ('2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'Citizenship', 'Unit 8', 'Molarum Grade 10 — Citizenship Unit 8: Globalization and Global Issues', 'Source-grounded Molarum Grade 10 Citizenship questions for Unit 8: Globalization and Global Issues.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET subject = EXCLUDED.subject, unit = EXCLUDED.unit, title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, quiz_id, question_type, question_text, correct_answer, explanation, order_index) VALUES ('c088af75-5c41-416d-8d81-c6fba2aa5c10'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'In the Zeleke case study, who did he include in the committee that managed to collect money and equipment for the school?', 'People from the community and the teachers of the school', 'The case study states he organized a committee that included people from the community and the teachers of the school, who then collected funds and equipment.', 0),('55e4dcfb-bd89-4bae-85df-b12c97262dbb'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which term from the glossary best describes the principle of relying on voluntary action or volunteers?', 'Voluntarism', 'The glossary defines ''Voluntarism'' as the principle or system of doing something by or relying on voluntary action or volunteers, matching the question.', 1),('3df68cd8-2717-436e-85dc-f3317ef6e8f4'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the unit summary, which phrase best defines patriotism?', 'Devotion to and vigorous support for one''s country', 'The glossary entry defines patriotism as ''Devotion to and vigorous support for one''s country,'' which directly answers the question.', 2),('7d8092ac-96ae-4bb0-8f0e-696f96bfb218'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which statement matches the textbook definition of globalization?', 'Globalization refers to the multiplicity of linkages and interconnections between states and societies making events in one place affect distant parts of the globe.', 'The excerpt defines globalization as multiplicity of linkages and interconnections so that events and activities in one part can have consequences in distant parts of the globe.', 3),('ed282503-fc90-4d80-8215-bb951978bf5d'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following is NOT listed as a dimension of globalization in the textbook?', 'Astronomical dimensions', 'The text lists political, economic, social and cultural dimensions; ''Astronomical dimensions'' is not mentioned and so is not a listed dimension.', 4),('7d8f7333-be92-4c90-8249-b4bf9a8a1c84'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which description matches the textbook''s economic dimension of globalization?', 'The increasing interdependence of world economies through cross-border trade, capital flows and technologies', 'The economic dimension is described as increasing interdependence of world economies via cross-border trade, capital flows and rapid spread of technologies, matching the chosen option.', 5),('b19d2c86-2dd8-4a40-8633-ce256babc416'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which social advantage of globalization is described in the textbook?', 'It turned education to be market oriented and enables labour to move across countries for jobs', 'Under social advantages the text explains globalization made education more market oriented and enabled labour to move between countries to get jobs and market products.', 6),('fe63f031-e71d-4d43-82ee-b8f45278a7b9'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which example does the textbook give to illustrate cultural diffusion under globalization?', 'The trading and global consumption of coffee, originally from Ethiopia', 'The text explicitly uses coffee, said to be originally from Ethiopia and now consumed globally, as an example of cultural diffusion through globalization.', 7),('a3d2ac59-58cf-4500-8204-28a7d698f00b'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which financial advantage of globalization is mentioned in the textbook?', 'It simplifies financial regulations and makes exchange of capital easier, for example by allowing remittances via money gram', 'The excerpt states that globalization simplifies financial regulations and facilitates exchange of capital, giving remittances through money gram as an example.', 8),('048e49d7-0d1c-4f30-82ab-a91bf5305d5a'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What cultural risk from globalization does the textbook describe?', 'Homogenization that can lead to disappearance of some cultures, languages and traditions', 'The text warns that cultural exchanges have homogenized cultures and that some cultures, languages and traditional practices are disappearing due to globalization.', 9),('c46441e5-19fe-46a8-887a-5eecf0581cfe'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which political disadvantage of globalization is given in the textbook?', 'It pressures leaders of developing countries to adopt measures sometimes opposite to their peoples'' sentiments, reinforcing authoritarianism', 'The excerpt explains globalization can pressure developing-country leaders to adopt policies opposite to popular sentiment, which may contribute to the rise of authoritarian regimes.', 10),('74e50ac2-1e12-4523-84bc-3fa556d6dbe1'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the textbook, how can globalization increase unemployment in developing countries?', 'By distorting production patterns toward capital-intensive methods instead of labour-intensive ones', 'The text states globalization can reduce indigenous technology development and promote capital-intensive production rather than labour-intensive methods, which in turn increases unemployment and poverty.', 11),('9f182c23-fbf9-4c3e-8204-69c5a6fa7dff'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which is an example of social insecurity due to globalization given in the textbook?', 'Illicit trade facilitated by deregulated markets and communication technologies', 'The excerpt notes that deregulated capital markets and advances in information and communications make illicit trades in drugs, women and weapons easier and contribute to crime and violence.', 12),('11ec6a38-0ad1-4dfa-8966-81951dce9f77'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which environmental consequence of globalization is mentioned in the textbook?', 'Increased greenhouse emissions and global warming from expanded transportation and industrial productivity', 'The excerpt links massive development in transportation and global economic growth to greenhouse emissions, global warming and environmental degradation.', 13),('44f56767-a74b-4a9e-89ab-5fb3c8a13a49'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What role does the textbook say promoting indigenous knowledge plays in countering negative impacts of globalization?', 'It values local practices and incorporates them into education to reduce dependence on externally produced knowledge', 'The text recommends incorporating indigenous knowledge into education so young people value local practices rather than depending solely on externally produced western knowledge.', 14),('379bc28c-c4a4-4807-8319-139ed8efe0c4'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Why does the textbook emphasize community development as a way to fight negative globalization impacts?', 'Because community participation creates ownership, responsibility and better project maintenance', 'The excerpt explains that community-based planning and execution create ownership and commitment, leading to better project maintenance and outcomes than externally designed programs.', 15),('d78b9cb2-8f85-4564-8fb6-725a9803312d'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of the following is listed as a protective social measure to reduce vulnerability in the textbook?', 'Regular cash transfers and public employment schemes', 'The text lists protective measures including basic transfers such as public employment schemes, school feeding and regular cash transfers to stop vulnerable groups from starving.', 16),('edf7cb1b-0cfd-4619-8e51-302303b8f15e'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'According to the textbook, regional cooperation can help fight negative impacts of globalization because it:', 'Intensifies cooperation among geographically related states and creates trade blocs and common policies for mutual gains', 'The text explains regional cooperation fosters political and economic cooperation, creating trade blocs and policies that help less developed countries address common problems.', 17),('72ce877a-8777-4489-85f7-5d3d479009d7'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'What is the purpose of the innovation fund suggested in the textbook?', 'To reward innovations that benefit developing countries and reduce costs of imported technology', 'The excerpt proposes a fund or prize system to reward valuable innovations useful to developing countries, helping them minimize costs of imported technological products.', 18),('05f207c4-2409-4d83-83e1-129938c969ca'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'multiple_choice', 'Which sentence best matches the textbook definition of a global issue?', 'An issue that arises when two or more states cannot agree on how to solve a problem and has potential to seriously impact the globe', 'The text defines global issues as those arising when two or more states cannot agree on solutions and any major trend or development that can seriously impact the globe.', 19),('ae50c17e-e9c7-4dd7-843f-531adaa86790'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'true_false', 'Global warming can cause sea level rise and increased frequency of droughts according to the textbook.', 'True', 'The excerpt lists sea level rise and increased frequency of droughts among the consequences of global warming, so the statement is true.', 20),('8dd870a1-19b0-4783-8d07-b2bba80e0f18'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The textbook states that poverty and inequality can have implications beyond national borders and thus are global problems.', 'True', 'The text explains poverty and inequality weaken states and have consequences for neighboring states and the global community, making them global problems.', 21),('07ea322f-de5f-4485-87cb-524c62abfd29'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The unit review states that history is part of social science that deals with social events.', 'True', 'One of the unit review True/False statements affirms that history is a social science dealing with social events, so this statement is true per the text.', 22),('57fee582-d93a-47fa-8dae-35af9390566f'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'true_false', 'The unit review claims selfish personal interests strengthen community spirit and joint effort for common purposes.', 'False', 'The unit review implies the opposite: selfish personal interests harm community spirit and joint effort, so the statement is false.', 23),('fae987e8-ea44-457b-8a13-4ec294989e99'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Define globalization as given in the textbook.', 'Globalization refers to the multiplicity of linkages and interconnections between the states and societies which make up the modern world system, so events and activities in one part of the world can have significant consequences for distant parts.', 'This answer restates the textbook definition that globalization involves linkages and interconnections causing distant consequences.', 24),('ac5591cf-2761-408f-8bcb-6000b3837748'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'List the dimensions of globalization mentioned in the textbook.', 'Political, economic, social and cultural dimensions.', 'The textbook explicitly lists these four dimensions as elements of the globalization process.', 25),('0557d8b5-4541-4dcf-8b90-11d2445c2138'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What is meant by a ''global issue'' according to the textbook?', 'A global issue is any major trend, shock, or development that can seriously impact the globe and arises when two or more states cannot agree on how to solve a problem.', 'The excerpt defines global issues as those that affect large parts of the globe and can arise from disagreements between states over solutions, with potential for serious impact.', 26),('64190e9a-9850-4df5-8349-ae6fe8882711'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Explain one economic advantage of globalization described in the textbook.', 'Globalization increases trade and economic exchange, fostering global economic growth and rapid industrial development that contribute to availability of technologies and commodities.', 'The economic advantages section explains globalization has led to increased trade and industrial development, which drives growth and technology availability.', 27),('0c11dcc0-e905-4045-8e8e-0c7e9c849bcc'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'Briefly describe why incorporating indigenous knowledge into education is recommended in the textbook.', 'Because indigenous knowledge arises from real-life experience, motivates people by valuing forebears'' knowledge, and helps reduce dependence on externally produced western knowledge.', 'The textbook argues indigenous knowledge should be included in education to value local creativity and reduce reliance on western models inappropriate to local contexts.', 28),('ed8db4be-ab2e-47d2-8f64-b5509a0bbffb'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What is one reason regional cooperation is viewed as effective against negative globalization impacts?', 'Regional cooperation allows states with comparable economic and cultural patterns to create trade blocs and common policies that address shared problems and foster productive capacities.', 'The text explains regionalism enables groups of nations to cooperate politically and economically, creating regional frameworks that address common problems more effectively.', 29),('da87223a-e6e5-41f4-81f5-82ac89e2fb64'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'According to the unit summary, why is patriotism important?', 'Patriotism creates a feeling of love, devotion and attachment to the homeland and alliance with other citizens, fostering a sense of oneness among the people.', 'The unit summary explains patriotism as love and attachment to the homeland and alliance with citizens, which creates oneness among people.', 30),('8c812029-3ef8-4730-80e7-5d5cfceefdac'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How does the textbook describe nationalism in modern history?', 'Nationalism is a movement that regards the nation state as paramount for realizing social, economic and cultural aspirations, characterized by communality based on descent, language and religion.', 'The unit summary defines nationalism as prioritizing the nation state and highlights its basis in common descent, language and religion as described in the excerpt.', 31),('18c9aa47-44ae-4eab-8859-e22c6793a39f'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many dimensions of globalization are explicitly listed in the textbook?', '4', 'The text enumerates four dimensions: political, economic, social and cultural, so the count is four.', 32),('85b8050f-b713-4a14-88f3-1e363ef1bf50'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many main categories of advantages of globalization are listed under section 8.2.1 (labeled a to e)?', '5', 'Advantages are presented under headings a through e (Economic, Political, Social, Cultural, Financial), totaling five categories.', 33),('d2a01e26-8409-4feb-8c92-1fcffecc5f99'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many ways/mechanisms of fighting the negative impacts of globalization are listed under section 8.3.1 (labeled a to e)?', '5', 'Section 8.3.1 lists five mechanisms labeled a to e: promoting indigenous knowledge, community development, indigenous social welfare, regional cooperation, and innovation fund.', 34),('2b8fca05-f7db-4d27-8260-77dfda4da013'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'What is the minimum whole birr amount explicitly reported as collected by the committee in the case study?', '200000', 'The case study states the committee managed to collect more than 200,000 birr, so the minimum whole amount explicitly reported is 200,000 birr.', 35),('805fda58-94f4-479d-85c1-1f694c8b3260'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many major global issues are introduced with lettered headings (A, B, C) in section 8.4?', '3', 'Section 8.4 introduces major global issues labeled A (Climate change), B (Poverty and inequality), and C (Population explosion), a total of three headings.', 36),('042569e5-0e19-421b-89f8-1477e6fc8847'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many main disadvantage subsections (labeled a to d) are listed under ''Disadvantages of globalization'' in section 8.2.2?', '4', 'The disadvantages are divided into four main subsections labeled a to d: Cultural loss, Political disadvantages, Economic effects, and Social insecurity, so the count is four.', 37),('f63981fb-140b-49b4-813a-8b34f886b649'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many bullet points are listed under the social advantages subsection (labeled c) in section 8.2.1?', '4', 'The social advantages subsection lists four bullet points describing transformations, market-oriented education, dispersion of ideas and improvements in technologies and living conditions.', 38),('fe6cf29b-ea2b-413e-8ba5-749ccdd99057'::uuid, '2c5b5dd1-a4bb-4e06-856f-8d686a8b92ff'::uuid, 'fill_blank', 'How many distinct effects of global warming are explicitly listed in the sentence beginning ''Global warming causes'' in the climate change subsection?', '8', 'The sentence lists sea level rise; increased frequency of droughts; submersion of towns and villages; decline in agriculture and fishing; frequent unusual weather; spread of infectious diseases; desertification; and decreasing biodiversity, totaling eight effects.', 39) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET quiz_id = EXCLUDED.quiz_id, question_type = EXCLUDED.question_type, question_text = EXCLUDED.question_text, correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, order_index = EXCLUDED.order_index;
